WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.175
This is the simplest quadratic: y equals x squared.

2
00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:11.900
Its graph is a parabola: a symmetric curve with one turning point, called the vertex.

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.850
The number in front of x squared is a.

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.800
Make a bigger, and the parabola gets narrower.

5
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.725
Make a smaller, and it opens out wider.

6
00:00:24.175 --> 00:00:28.083
And if a is negative, the parabola flips upside down:

7
00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:31.600
it now has a maximum instead of a minimum.

8
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.075
The constant term, c, slides the whole curve up and down.

9
00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:41.250
It is also where the graph crosses the y-axis.

10
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:48.543
The roots are where the curve meets the x-axis. For x squared minus two x minus three,

11
00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:50.800
they are minus one and three.

12
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.292
The discriminant, b squared minus four a c,

13
00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:58.475
tells you how many roots there are before you draw anything.

14
00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:04.631
Positive: two roots. Zero: the curve just touches the axis. Negative:

15
00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.225
it misses the axis completely.
